faceDelete -- computes the face deletion for a simplicial complex
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        faceDelete(F, S)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a face of $S$
      * S, an *note abstract simplicial complex:
        (SimplicialComplexes)SimplicialComplex,,
  * Outputs:
      * T, an *note abstract simplicial complex:
        (SimplicialComplexes)SimplicialComplex,, the simplicial complex of all
        faces in $S$ not containing the face $F$

Description
===========

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e];                              |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = simplicialComplex {a*b*c*d*e};         |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : faceDelete(a, S)                           |
|                                                |
|o3 = simplicialComplex | bcde |                 |
|                                                |
|o3 : SimplicialComplex                          |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : faceDelete(a*b*c, S)                       |
|                                                |
|o4 = simplicialComplex | bcde acde abde |       |
|                                                |
|o4 : SimplicialComplex                          |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : faceDelete(a*b*c*d*e, S) === skeleton(3, S)|
|                                                |
|o5 = true                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Do not confuse face deletion with normal deletion wherein the vertices of the
given face are entirely removed.

