isSheddingVertex -- determines whether a vertex of a simplicial complex is a shedding vertex
********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isSheddingVertex(x, S)
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a vertex of $S$
      * S, an *note abstract simplicial complex:
        (SimplicialComplexes)SimplicialComplex,,
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if and only if
        $x$ is a shedding vertex of $S$

Description
===========

Definition 11.1 of [BW-2] states that a shedding vertex $x$ of a simplicial
complex $S$ is a vertex such that the link and face deletion of $x$ from $S$
are vertex decomposable and share no common facets.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..f];                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = simplicialComplex {a*b*c, c*d, d*e, e*f, d*f};|
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isSheddingVertex(a, S)                            |
|                                                       |
|o3 = false                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isSheddingVertex(f, S)                            |
|                                                       |
|o4 = true                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note faceDelete: faceDelete, -- computes the face deletion for a
    simplicial complex
  * *note isVertexDecomposable: isVertexDecomposable, -- determines whether a
    simplicial complex is vertex-decomposable
  * *note link: (SimplicialComplexes)link_lpSimplicialComplex_cmRingElement_rp,
    -- make the link of a face in an abstract simplicial complex

