isShelling -- determines whether a list of faces is a shelling
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isShelling L
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of faces (i.e., squarefree
        monic monomials)
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if and only if
        $L$ is shelling

Description
===========

Determines if a list of faces is a shelling order of the simplicial complex
generated by the list.

Let $S$ be the simplicial complex generated by the list of facets $L$.  If $S$
is pure, then definition III.2.1 in [St] is used. That is, $L_1, .., L_n$ is a
shelling order of $S$ if the difference in the $j$-th and $j-1$-th subcomplex
has a unique minimal face, for $2 \leq j \leq n$.

If $S$ is non-pure, then definition 2.1 in [BW-1] is used.  That is, $L_1, ..,
L_n$ is a shelling order if the intersection of the faces of the first $j-1$
facets with the faces of the $L_j$ is pure and $dim L_j - 1$-dimensional.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..e];                   |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : isShelling {a*b*c, b*c*d, c*d*e}|
|                                     |
|o2 = true                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : isShelling {a*b*c, c*d*e, b*c*d}|
|                                     |
|o3 = false                           |
+-------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isShellable: isShellable, -- determines whether a simplicial complex
    is shellable
  * *note shellingOrder: shellingOrder, -- finds a shelling of a simplicial
    complex, if one exists

